# Fantasy mobile design

Read `docs/PRODUCT.md` and the matching living-surface row first. The approved reference is `docs/mockups/fantasy-mobile-home-a.html` (September 29, 2026). Reuse its controls and spacing; keep each destination's own content hierarchy. Strategy, Rosters, live Draft, My team, and Game center retain their approved board/table/room structures.

## Start from the shared foundation

- Static mocks load `mockup-shared.css`, then `mobile-foundation.css`, then page-specific styles. Start with `_mobile-starter.html` through `scripts/dev/mobile_mock.py`; instructions live in `.cursor/skills/fast-ui-mock/SKILL.md`.
- Production uses existing `MobileHeader`, `MobileShell`, `HubUILayout` and the product token/phone styles. Mock classes are examples, not a second production design system.
- Change shared controls in the foundation and recheck its consumers. Keep phase logic, scoring, chat content, and task ordering in each page's own files.

## Parameters at phone widths (≤768px)

| Role | Mock token / default |
|------|----------------------|
| Page inset | `--mobile-page-inset`: 16px |
| Card inset | `--mobile-card-inset`: 16px |
| Section gap | `--mobile-section-gap`: 16px |
| Header/control gap | `--mobile-header-gap`: 12px |
| Touch target | `--mobile-touch-target`: 44px minimum |
| Control icon | `--mobile-control-icon`: 20px; intrinsic SVG width/height required |
| Card radius | `--mobile-card-radius`: 18px |
| Bottom clearance | `--mobile-nav-clearance`: 6rem + safe-area inset |

These alias existing ScoreSense tokens. Type stays ≥12px; text inputs use 16px. Use the established palette and type scale. Desktop density follows `frontend-craft.mdc`.

## Chrome, alignment, and controls

- At desktop widths, anchor the league switcher to the left of its context row, aligned with the page content. Keep the compact phone header arrangement below 769px.

- New Fantasy phone mocks start with one row: destination left and quieter league switcher toward the right, with an internal text inset. More belongs only in the bottom navigation. Aim for the approved 61px header, ≤72px in the audit. Keep long names truncated with full accessible labels and both switch actions reachable. Do not stack centered Home/league pills or repeat the league strip on phone.
- The phone destination picker mirrors desktop primary destinations plus League. Secondary pages (Vibes, Cap, Rules, etc.) live under League with the same permission and capability filters as desktop.
- Center short card headings, matchups, and standalone key figures. Left-align navigation, message text, player lists, forms, and actionable issues. Table numbers and their headers stay right-aligned.
- Disclosures use a small leading icon, concise centered title, and a 44px plus/minus state indicator. Use native `details/summary`; keep summary `display: list-item`, put the grid inside, and hide its native marker only when providing the visible replacement. Never nest a second button in summary.
- Make controls feel responsive with clear selected, expanded, pressed, and focus states. Respect reduced motion. Use accent for current selection and a meaningful next action; neutral controls can carry the rest. A page can have no primary action.
- Keep Projections / Fantasy / Tools / More at the bottom, with safe-area padding and content clearance. Preview labels and scenario controls sit outside product chrome.

## Content discipline

- Put the page's useful decision or content first. Omit repeated titles, explanations of familiar fantasy tasks, decorative metrics, and empty sections. Add a short support line only when it changes understanding.
- Disclose secondary detail. Keep urgent blocking issues visible beside the affected action; a collapsed section must not hide a blocker.
- Phase relevance matters: show only the money, dates, and actions that matter in the current state. Home's in-season/pre-draft ordering and Wednesday transition live in its registry row and `PRODUCT.md`; they are not defaults for every page.

## Preview checks

At 390 and 1280: run the layout audit and inspect screenshots. At 320: check long destination/league names, touch targets, and overflow. Exercise pickers, disclosure click/keyboard behavior, relevant phases, and fixed-nav clearance. Audit success does not replace visual inspection.

After any CSS/JS change, run `mobile_mock.py stamp` on affected pages, then reload the user's existing preview tab when available. Version every direct local stylesheet/script, including the foundation; a fresh screenshot session alone can miss stale styles in an already-open tab.
